tolerant of others. Is it more because they just realize that every person is an individual and they're able to recognize that? I'm curious what your research has shown. Yeah, that's exactly right. And at this point that connection is, little bit more theoretical than some of these other findings. In general, if you look cross-culturally, individualistic cultures do tend to be more tolerant. But there's not as much work on that as you'd expect. So that's something that's kind of an area for future research. But in terms of the trends over time, it's very clear that there's much more gender equality, racial equality, equality based on sexual orientation, all of these things have increased in our culture in the last 50 years
包容他人有关。是因为他们意识到每个人都是独立的个体，并且能够认识到这一点吗？我很好奇您的研究显示了什么。是的，完全正确。在这一点上，这种联系比其他一些发现更具理论性。总的来说，如果你进行跨文化观察，个人主义文化确实往往更具包容性。但关于这方面的研究并没有你预期的那么多。所以这是未来研究的一个领域。但就随时间变化的趋势而言，很明显，性别平等、种族平等、基于性取向的平等，所有这些在过去50年里在我们的文化中都有所增加。

9
00:05:22.000 --> 00:06:08.000
or so. Just enormous amounts of change, things that used to be taken for granted as social rules are no longer. And many of those changes are really beneficial in that they're treating people as individuals rather than members of groups, that you can see someone as for who they are, rather than saying, well, you're a woman, so you need to do this, or you're gay so you can't get married. Those attitudes are not as accepted anymore. And that's one of those positive things about this cultural shift toward more individualism. I'm curious, and I don't know how far back your research goes as far as generations, but it seems like things are moving faster, and social change is moving faster.
大约50年左右。发生了巨大的变化，曾经被视为理所当然的社会规则已不再适用。其中许多变化确实是有益的，因为它们将人们视为个体而非群体成员，你可以看到一个人的本质，而不是说“好吧，你是女性，所以你需要做这个”或者“你是同性恋，所以你不能结婚”。这些态度不再被广泛接受。这就是这种向个人主义转变的文化中积极的一面。我很好奇，我不知道您的研究在代际方面追溯到了多远，但似乎事情发展得更快了，社会变革正在加速。

10
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Comparatively, I'm talking about hundreds of years. I mean, are we looking at in the last 50 years or so a more dramatic shift? Or is it changing slowly more steadily over time? You know, I think it depends on the particular trade or attitude. You know, it varies. So I think for individualism, there's been a lot of other authors who have made this case, too, about individualism increasing. And at least one says individualism has probably been increasing in Western nations since the Renaissance.
相比之下，我指的是几百年的跨度。我的意思是，我们是在观察过去50年左右发生的更剧烈的转变吗？还是它在随时间缓慢而稳定地变化？我认为这取决于具体的特征或态度。我认为，对于个人主义，也有很多其他作者提出了同样的观点，即个人主义正在增加。至少有一位作者认为，自文艺复兴以来，个人主义可能一直在西方国家增加。

11
