But he argues that that really took off, really accelerated beginning in the 1970s. And that's certainly what the data seems to look at, too, like some of those Google Book Studies. That's when a lot of these changes really took place. But it really does vary. A lot of the generational changes in terms of these positive self-use, they happened in the 1970s and 1980s and then have leveled off. Same thing for some of the increases in anxiety and depression.
但他认为，这种趋势在20世纪70年代开始真正起飞并加速。这当然也是数据所呈现的样子，比如那些谷歌图书研究。那时许多变化确实发生了。但它确实存在差异。许多关于积极自我评价的代际变化发生在20世纪70年代和80年代，然后趋于平稳。焦虑和抑郁的增加也是如此。

12
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:37.000
But then there's other areas, say like equal rights for gays and lesbians, or equal rights for women where there was a lot of change in the 70s. And then again, there was kind of a plateau in the 80s and 90s, and then just since 2000, there's been more change. So there's some interesting patterns. It's not always completely in one direction. There's times when there's lulls in the progress or lulls in the trend. But we're definitely living in a time now shaped by technology
但也有其他领域，比如男女同性恋的平等权利，或者女性的平等权利，在70年代发生了很大变化。然后在80年代和90年代出现了一种停滞，自2000年以来又发生了更多变化。所以有一些有趣的模式。它并不总是完全朝一个方向发展。有时进步或趋势会出现停滞。但我们现在确实生活在一个由技术塑造的时代。

13
00:07:37.000 --> 00:08:06.000
in these things which may be accelerating cultural change. And I think that's another great area for future. your research too, is to find out which eras have the most change and, you know, have things really accelerated. Why is it important for companies and organizations to understand the characteristics or the personalities of their employees and, you know, the generational differences that come into play in the workplace? It's really crucial to have a view of which differences among those young workers that
这些事物可能会加速文化变革。我认为这也是未来研究的一个很好的领域，即找出哪些时代变化最大，以及事情是否真的加速了。为什么企业和组织了解员工的特征或个性，以及职场中出现的代际差异很重要？了解这些年轻员工中出现的差异是非常关键的……

14
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:20.000
you're seeing. Which of those are really due to generation and which of those are due to age? because you can look at those young workers and you can think, man, I never did that. I never showed up late for work. But really? Really? Is that really true?
你所看到的。哪些真正归因于代际，哪些归因于年龄？因为你可以看着那些年轻员工，心想：“天哪，我从来没那样做过。我从不迟到。”但真的吗？真的吗？那真的是事实吗？

15
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:44.000
I'm sure you probably did, and you probably just have this rosy view of the past. So what we really need is to try to find data that compares these young workers now to what young workers used to be like, say, in the 1990s or in the 1970s. That'll show us if they're really our generational or time period differences, or whether it's just due to being young or, due to your memory being faulty or some other thing.
我相信你可能也做过，你可能只是对过去有一种玫瑰色的滤镜。所以我们真正需要的是尝试寻找数据，将现在的年轻员工与20世纪90年代或70年代的年轻员工进行比较。这将向我们展示这是否真的是代际或时间段的差异，还是仅仅因为年轻，或者是因为你的记忆有误或其他原因。

