they thought that work was going to be a less central part of their lives. So this all suggests, you know, just as one thing that managers really need to understand, that this generation that they're seeing in the workplace, that, yeah, they'll do good work for you, but they really, really crave that flexibility and they want to be able to have work-life balance and be able to have their lives outside of work as well. And that was a reasonably big difference. That was more than half a standard deviation because there's been some skeptics who have said, oh, you know, yes, there's some differences, but really, you know, they're pretty small. Well, that's a reasonably big difference.
他们认为工作在他们生活中所占的比重会降低。所以这一切都表明，正如管理者真正需要理解的一点，他们所看到的这一代职场新人，是的，他们会为你做好工作，但他们确实非常渴望灵活性，他们希望能够实现工作与生活的平衡，并能够在工作之外拥有自己的生活。这是一个相当大的差异。这超过了半个标准差，因为有一些怀疑论者说：“哦，是的，确实有一些差异，但实际上它们很小。”好吧，这是一个相当大的差异。

